The POST /run_sse streaming endpoint works by: (1) accepting request body with appName, userId, sessionId, newMessage, streaming (boolean), and stateDelta fields, (2) validating the session exists (returns 404 if not found), (3) setting SSE headers: Cache-Control: 'no-cache', Content-Type: 'text/event-stream', Access-Control-Allow-Origin: '*', Connection: 'keep-alive', (4) calling res.flushHeaders() to send headers immediately, (5) running the agent with runConfig: {streamingMode: streaming ? StreamingMode.SSE : StreamingMode.NONE}, (6) for each event from the async generator, writing to response as: res.write(`data: ${JSON.stringify(event)}

`), (7) calling res.end() when complete. If an error occurs after headers are sent, it writes the error as an SSE event: res.end(`data: ${JSON.stringify({error: message})}

`). If headers haven't been sent, it returns 500 status with JSON error. The streaming flag controls whether partial events are yielded during model generation.

